comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T05:08:41.357Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for multi round-trip input_required inputRequests inputResponses elicitation retry requestState and reverse RPC removal. No canonical MCP MRTR owner exists."
body: "## State model\n\n- A handler either returns complete or input_required.\n- input_required contains ordered typed inputRequests and opaque requestState bounded by policy.\n- The host retries the original method with inputResponses and the exact application state needed to continue.\n- URL-mode elicitation learns completion through retry and carries correlation only in requestState.\n- Cancellation, idempotency, replay protection, expiration, redaction, and consent are explicit.\n- pm recovery envelopes can map missing authority or missing user choices into safe MRTR requests without weakening refusal semantics."
